+## CL39 BA-start-10 full-panel validation
+
+On 27 August 2026, the sealed CL39 24k checkpoint was replayed on all 96 seed-0
+`manual_val` cells with the only scientific change at inference being
+`validation_args.branched_attn_start_step=10` instead of 15. The model-level
+start remains 15 to preserve the checkpoint architecture contract. An isolated
+equality-boundary fix makes equal PM/BA starts enter `BOTH` at step 10; focused
+assertions preserve the original PM-only 10-14 / BOTH 15-49 schedule. The
+successful one-A100 full-panel job is
+`lm-mpi-job-8ca02579-79d3-4c94-9515-a50bcde5b9c1` (`Completed`, platform
+error code zero, 2,058 seconds), with exactly 96 accepted images, gate SHA-256
+`32ad29cd77fcfd10980d52570732f41fbfa7d8b040c2fafe75e46187edc734ae`,
+and source-manifest SHA-256
+`07a09a43aee5090fc87c089a948a2d353c4f72e10fc3f259b465d337e33cd507`.
+
+On the fixed-box subject-v2 metric, BA@10 versus BA@15 changes intended ID by
+`-0.00779` (95% fixed-cell bootstrap interval `[-0.01632,+0.00044]`; 35/96
+wins), next/wrong ID by `-0.00218`, and identity margin by `-0.00562`; all
+intervals include zero. Intended ID declines for six of eight identities and
+losses outnumber gains 61 to 35. Both arms have zero no-face, unowned and
+ambiguous cells; fixed-box IoU changes only `-0.00168`. Retain the original
+BA@15 schedule. This full-panel result supersedes the earlier Eddie-only
+population estimate while preserving its decision; Eddie's exact 12-cell
+means remain reproducible in the larger result.
+
+CL39 training itself uses `train_ba_all_steps=true` with
+`ba_training_timestep_policy=uniform_all`: BA trains on uniformly sampled
+timesteps across the full training diffusion schedule. The original 35/50 BA
+steps are an inference suffix, not a training fraction. The superseding
+auditable report is `analysis/2026-08-27_cl39_ba_start10_full96.md`; its
+visually verified six-page local PDF is
